From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the PWM controllers

The A733 has two PWM controllers with ten channels each, which the
device tree does not describe. Add pwm0 and pwm1, disabled, and one pin
group for each PWM1 pin on the Radxa Cubie A7S header J11 used here
(PD11 to PD13, PJ22 to PJ25) and for the blue LED (PJ26). The values
(page numbers are pages of the A733 manual PDF):

- Registers at 0x02527000 (PWM0) and 0x02528000 (PWM1), 4 KiB each in
  the memory map (p.26). The last register is at 0x364, so the size is
  0x400.
- Interrupts 67 and 68, which are GIC_SPI 35 and 36: interrupt table
  (section 12.2.3.1, p.614).
- Ten channels each: PWM0_[9:0] and PWM1_[9:0] (section 18.7.1).
- Clocks: the bus gate, SYS_CLK24M and APB0 as hosc and apb. The
  manual gives SYS_CLK24M as a fixed 24 MHz clock from PLL_REF, not
  the 26 MHz DCXO (section 18.7.3, p.1323). Reset: RST_BUS_PWM0 and
  RST_BUS_PWM1.
- PD11, PD12 and PD13 carry PWM1-1, PWM1-2 and PWM1-3 on function 7
  (PD_CFG1, p.1647). PJ22 to PJ26 carry PWM1-4 to PWM1-8 on function 3
  (PJ_CFG2, PJ_CFG3, p.1764 to 1766).

The board connects PD11 to PD13 and PJ22 to PJ25 to the 30-pin header
J11 (schematic V1.10, sheet 14) and PJ26 to the blue LED (sheet 16).
PJ27, which carries PWM1-9, goes to the fan connector J7, which is not
fitted, so it has no group. The nodes stay disabled and the pin groups
are /omit-if-no-ref/, because nothing fitted on the board uses them.

Not covered: enabling a controller on the board, S_PWM, and the PWM0
pins.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board with pwm1 enabled and
the PJ26 group selected in a test device tree; the controller probes
with ten channels, PJ26 takes its PWM function and the LED blinks.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 80 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 80 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index b9e48dbcbdad..d520847695b2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -597,6 +597,62 @@ mmc2_pins: mmc2-pins {
 				bias-pull-up;
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pd11_pin: pwm1-pd11-pin {
+				pins = "PD11";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <7>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pd12_pin: pwm1-pd12-pin {
+				pins = "PD12";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <7>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pd13_pin: pwm1-pd13-pin {
+				pins = "PD13";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <7>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pj22_pin: pwm1-pj22-pin {
+				pins = "PJ22";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pj23_pin: pwm1-pj23-pin {
+				pins = "PJ23";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pj24_pin: pwm1-pj24-pin {
+				pins = "PJ24";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pj25_pin: pwm1-pj25-pin {
+				pins = "PJ25";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			pwm1_pj26_pin: pwm1-pj26-pin {
+				pins = "PJ26";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "pwm1";
+			};
+
 			/omit-if-no-ref/
 			rgmii0_ph_pins: rgmii0-ph-pins {
 				pins = "PH0", "PH1", "PH2", "PH4", "PH5",
@@ -843,6 +899,30 @@ lradc: lradc@2524000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		pwm0: pwm@2527000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm";
+			reg = <0x02527000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 35 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_PWM0>, <&ccu CLK_SYS_24M>, <&ccu CLK_APB0>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "hosc", "apb";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_PWM0>;
+			#pwm-cells = <3>;
+			allwinner,npwms = <10>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		pwm1: pwm@2528000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm";
+			reg = <0x02528000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 36 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_PWM1>, <&ccu CLK_SYS_24M>, <&ccu CLK_APB0>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "hosc", "apb";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_PWM1>;
+			#pwm-cells = <3>;
+			allwinner,npwms = <10>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		syscon: syscon@3000000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-system-control";
 			reg = <0x03000000 0x1000>;
